 # What the calculator is for
 
-The calculator lists shorter radiotherapy schedules for head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) whose modeled doses stay close to the standard 70 Gy in 35 fractions of 2 Gy over 47 days. It is a tool for designing trials and generating hypotheses. A listed schedule is a candidate for a trial, not an equivalent schedule and not a treatment recommendation. Site: https://ishuryak.shinyapps.io/custom_bed_calculator_v4/ (the page footer and the Model and sources page give the version and the deployed revision). The main page is "Suggested regimens". The menu opens Check a regimen, Custom search (advanced), Uncertainty, Organs at risk, and Settings and sources (with the tabs Model settings and Model and sources). The guide for version 3.2.1 (`HNSCC_BED_v321_user_guide.md`) is kept as a historical record and does not describe this layout.
+The calculator lists shorter radiotherapy schedules for head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) whose modeled doses stay close to the standard 70 Gy in 35 fractions of 2 Gy over 47 days. It is a tool for designing trials and generating hypotheses. A listed schedule is a candidate for a trial, not an equivalent schedule and not a treatment recommendation. Site: https://ishuryak.shinyapps.io/custom_bed_calculator_v4/ (the page footer and the Model and sources page give the version and the deployed revision). The main page is "Suggested regimens". The menu opens Check a regimen, Custom search (advanced), Uncertainty, Organs at risk, How the models were fitted (Bayesian), and Settings and sources (with the tabs Model settings and Model and sources). The guide for version 3.2.1 (`HNSCC_BED_v321_user_guide.md`) is kept as a historical record and does not describe this layout.
 
